{
  "id": "ss.enemy.bristle",
  "name": "Bristle",
  "description": "The burrow's fast chaff, and the only thing down here that does not belong to the hive — a silverfish living in the wall seams, running the trails and stealing off them. Drawn from directly above and along +x, because the game turns this body to its heading instead of flipping it: a top-down creature has no up to preserve, and where it is pointing is the whole read. Threaded at both ends — three tail filaments behind, two feelers ahead — so the silhouette is a spindle with hair on it, not the Drifter's wide bright wings. Deliberately the palest body on the roster: the earth it runs on is #372d3f and the fastest thing on screen must never be the hardest to see. Gameplay radius 7.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "bristle"],
  "size": [36, 24],
  "meta": {"radius": 7},
